er surveys pointed the same direction.\n\nExpert raters are split between Tossup and Democratic-leaning calls, and prediction markets give Stelson roughly an 80 percent chance of winning. Perry's name recognition and the district's Republican lean keep the seat within reach for the incumbent, and coverage of dissident Republican voters suggests the electorate could still break his way. This remains a genuine flip opportunity but not a safe one for either side.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7335, "margin": 3.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7265, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7615, "margin": 4.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7786, "margin": 4.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7238, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7163, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7699, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7923, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7321, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7447, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7423, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7477, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7786, "margin": 4.2}]}